wer Heinkel  cabina micro cars and decided to improve  on the design with a door in the front  and a bit more power he's proud that the  only two cylinder car in the field won  third place two years ago he's hoping to  repeat that this year but says it'll  depend on his co-driver he says it's  great here and many of the rallies you  have to constantly watch your location  while here he'll be able to get a  glimpse of the landscape  afterwards the cars will be presented at  a high-caliber Concord elegance but some  of the participants have found the rally  quite exhausting she says she felt a lot  of pressure because her husband takes  the whole thing quite seriously  she herself drives for fun while he is  more ambitious but she says they're  happy to be here Arthur tells us about  their car the opel admiral was built in  1938 when the body by Glaser  he says the special thing about this  model is that the top is completely  retractable compared to beetle tops with  their giant bulge he says the car was  discovered as a towing vehicle in  Montevideo there was a crane sticking  out of the back axis after much  searching he was able to find an  original car radio from 1938  the confession you got a massage  this 1953 Goliath sport is the first  series vehicle with direct  fuel-injection the two cylinder engine  and this elegant sporty coupe a only  reaches 32 horsepower but since the car  only weighs 830 kilograms and gets a  dynamic 120 km/h there are only two of  them left today each of these vehicles  has a special atmosphere and a special  story that the owners are happy to tell  a horse 8:53 from 1935 this convertible  was a sporty addition to horses palette  of clunky upper-class saloon cars the  Kaba  I'm the Montford shrugs tells us how he  commissioned an English vintage car  dealer to find a model like this the man  didn't even know the horse brand existed  if he asked Porsche how do you spell it  and then he located it in a barn in Ohio  an American general had brought it to  the US after World War two and driven it  around until 1953 you believe Tata meet  cotton born in u.s. are on this town of  Bastogne saloon the driving from fatigue  a farm bought the horse 8:53 was  considered one of the most beautiful  cars of its time after seven years of  work it's been restored to its former  glory  it gets reactions very different from  the BMW 602 de says a woman told him how  she and her husband drove to Italy on  their honeymoon in this car 56 years ago  he says it's practical for old people to  reawaken youthful memories  which may explain why it's drivers get  the jury special price for the most  original vehicle at this year's loss  bents bag classics
 

